// The iron spit, and the two things it is for.
//
// The spit is smithed from an iron bar at 17 Smithing and then, before this, did nothing at all -
// the playtest report's "iron spit - nothing interesting happens". Its use is cooking: thread raw
// meat onto it and the skewered meat goes on a fire. Raw rabbit was the other half of the same
// dead end - it drops from every rabbit and the charter shop stocks twenty of them, and there was
// no way to cook one. Both the skewered rabbit and the roast rabbit have been sitting in the 377
// cache since 20 February 2006, models and all, waiting for these few lines.
//
// The spit is a tool, not an ingredient: it stays in the inventory, so one spit does a whole
// trip's worth of rabbits. https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Iron_spit
//
// The cooking half is an ordinary cooking_generic row (skill_cooking/configs/cooking_source), so
// the skewered rabbit goes through the same burn curve, batch loop and Cook-X window as any other
// food, and only over a fire - a range has nowhere to rest a spit. Eating the roast needs nothing
// new: the opheld audit already gave it a handler and a 7-hitpoint heal, and the Hitpoints guide
// has listed it all along. The food simply could not be reached.
//
// THE CHOMPY IS THE SAME DEAD END, reported separately (DeathPlateau-Bugs#77) and found the same
// way. spit_skewered_chompy has been in the 377 cache all along with a model, a name and obj id
// 7230 - the id Old School itself uses for it - and nothing in the build reached it, so the only
// route the wiki documents for cooking a chompy did not exist. Old School: use an iron spit on a
// raw chompy, then the skewered chompy on a FIRE, Cooking 30, for a cooked chompy or a ruined one.
// https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Skewered_chompy
//
// ONE PAIR, EITHER WAY ROUND, and that is already handled: raw_chompy has an [opheldu,raw_chompy]
// of its own for the chompy seasonings, and "use a on b" reaches only one of the two triggers. Its
// case list does not include the spit, so it falls to ~displaymessage(^dm_default) - which is the
// one place a script says "these two do not go together" and hands the click to the other half
// (misc/scripts/displaymessage.rs2). So the case below answers both directions.
//
// IT IS NOT A RECIPE FOR DISASTER STEP HERE. Our Freeing Skrach Uglogwee wants a cooked JUBBLY on
// the platter, which is the dish Old School hands over too, and the journal says so at every stage
// - the skewered chompy is Old School's way onto the boat back from Karamja, and ours is a boat the
// player hollows out with an axe. This fixes the dead end, not a blocked quest.
[opheldu,spit_iron]
switch_obj(last_useitem) {
    case raw_rabbit :
        inv_del(inv, raw_rabbit, 1);
        inv_add(inv, spit_skewered_rabbit_meat, 1);
        mes("You skewer the rabbit on the iron spit.");
    case raw_chompy :
        inv_del(inv, raw_chompy, 1);
        inv_add(inv, spit_skewered_chompy, 1);
        mes("You skewer the chompy on the iron spit.");
    case default : ~displaymessage(^dm_default);
}
